J-1: the CSV export neutralises text a spreadsheet would run as a formula with a leading
apostrophe, and the record import did not remove it, so exporting customers and importing them
again changed a phone number (+1 555 0100 -> '+1 555 0100), a note starting with a dash, and a
name starting with a dash. Added unguardCsvCell (src/lib/csv.ts), applied once at the top of the
import's value reader; a genuinely apostrophe-led name ('Round Table Ltd) is unchanged.

J-2: QBOMigrationWizard hand-rolled a CSV parser. Executed against the shared reader's inputs it
split a memo containing a line break into a second row, deleted doubled quotes, kept a European
semicolon export as one column, and accepted a truncated file silently. It now uses
parseCsvChecked from src/lib/csv.ts.

Tests: src/tests/j1-export-import-roundtrip.test.ts (4), src/tests/j2-qbo-migration-shared-csv.test.ts (5),
focused import/export regressions 92/92. Probes kept in audit/agent11/probes/.

