+# Agent #11 — checkpoint 01 — 10 November 2026
+
+**Lane (docs/COORDINATION.md):** AI #11 — *imports, exports and documents* (no change to how money is
+posted). Queue **J-1 … J-8**. Plus the owner's standing request in this session: the **final, accurate
+list** of open items, and permanent preservation of the work (Git + Google Drive).
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Repo | `Chaim-Richard/ledgerflow` (fork; push here, PR into `shmuelbiller1/ledgerflow:main`) |
+| Branch | `arena/37ddbc4d-ledgerflow` |
+| Base commit of this session | `e58fa00a75b22af5b93e8af85d379c94441781d3` |
+| Commit for this checkpoint | `ec71e2a2` — J-1 + J-2 fixes, probes, tests |
+| Upstream main read at start | `5968faf3` (10 Nov 2026) — 3,008 commits ahead of the checkout, used as a **read-only reference** (`git archive` to `/tmp/latest`) |
+| Drive folder | `Ledgerflow Agent11 audit 2026-11-10` — id `1wvRkM9OJbdRfu7QC48dD5dMSMTE_LEOr` |
+
+## What I read first
+
+`AGENTS.md`, `CURRENT_WORK.md`, `docs/COORDINATION.md` (the "AI #11: tasks" queue, J-1…J-8, written by
+Claude on 8 Nov), `docs/INDEPENDENT_AUDIT_AGENT.md`, the existing audit corpus (`audit/FINAL_ACCURATE_LIST_2026-10-25/27/28/29`,
+`audit/FINAL_ACCURATE_LIST_2026-11-08.md`, agent 6/7/8 checkpoints), the open issue list (15 open issues),
+and the open PRs on the fork.
+
+## Environment facts established (not assumed)
+
+- Local checkout is a **grafted single-commit snapshot** of 9 Nov; `upstream/main` is 3,008 commits
+  ahead and its tree differs by only **114 paths**. The source used for the audit is the checkout; upstream
+  main was used to see what has merged since (e.g. UX-5…UX-9, Sonar batches, audit reports from agents 7/8).
+- `npm ci` OK (1,206 packages). `npx tsc --noEmit` **clean** (0 errors) on the untouched checkout.
+- Full unit suite started from the untouched checkout: still running at this checkpoint — **750+ tests,
+  0 failures** at the time of writing. Final figure goes in checkpoint 02.
+- Repo has a corrupt committed file: **`audit/FINAL_ACCURATE_LIST_2026-11-08.md` contains unresolved Git
+  conflict markers** (`<<<<<<< HEAD` line 1, `=======` line 59, `>>>>>>> e9d5ae64 …` line 194) on
+  `upstream/main`. Recorded as a finding; it is agent #7/#4 territory to repair, not mine.
+
+## Findings so far in my lane (imports / exports / documents)
+
+### J-1 — export → import round trip changed the data. **FIXED, tested, pushed.**
+
+Mechanism: `sanitizeCsvCell` (src/lib/csv.ts) writes a leading apostrophe in front of any text a
+spreadsheet would run as a formula (`=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, tab, CR). Every CSV export goes through it. The
+record import (Settings → Import data) had no matching step, so re-importing an exported customer list
+changed the values:
+
+| Value as stored | Cell in the exported CSV | Value after import (before the fix) |
+|---|---|---|
+| `+1 555 0100` | `'+1 555 0100` | `'+1 555 0100` |
+| `-call before 10am` (note) | `'-call before 10am` | `'-call before 10am` |
+| `-Discount Customer` (name) | `'-Discount Customer` | `'-Discount Customer` |
+| `+972 3 555 0101` | `'+972 3 555 0101` | `'+972 3 555 0101` |
+
+Reproduction: `audit/agent11/probes/j1-export-roundtrip.ts` and `j1b-roundtrip-cleanup.ts` (executed).
+The import's own clean-up (`cleanupContactImportRows`) does not remove it, so the screen path also changed it.
+
+Fix: `unguardCsvCell` in `src/lib/csv.ts` removes exactly the guard this app wrote and nothing else
+(a real name beginning with an apostrophe, `'Round Table Ltd`, is untouched; a plain number `-1,000.00`,
+which was never guarded, is untouched). Applied once, at the top of `readValue` in
+`src/lib/recordImport.ts`, so every import field and both the preview and the server-side check see the
+same corrected text. Tests: `src/tests/j1-export-import-roundtrip.test.ts` (4).
+
+### J-2 — the QuickBooks Online migration wizard did not use the shared CSV reader. **FIXED, tested, pushed.**
+
+`src/components/migration/QBOMigrationWizard.tsx` hand-rolled a CSV parser (a split on line breaks, then a
+character loop). Executed side by side with `src/lib/csv.ts` (`audit/agent11/probes/j2-qbo-wizard-csv.ts`):
+
+| Input | Wizard (before) | Shared reader |
+|---|---|---|
+| memo with a line break in quotes | **split into two rows** (`first line` / `second line`) | one cell `first line\nsecond line` |
+| `"He said ""paid"" today"` | `He said paid today` (quotes **deleted**) | `He said "paid" today` |
+| European `;` export | one column `2026-01-05;Acme;paid` | three columns |
+| truncated file (unclosed quote) | accepted silently | `parseCsvChecked` refuses with a message |
+
+Effect on a real migration: a QuickBooks memo/description that contains a line break shifts every later
+column of that row, and a dropped quote silently alters imported text. Fix: the wizard now calls
+`parseCsvChecked` from `src/lib/csv.ts`. Tests: `src/tests/j2-qbo-migration-shared-csv.test.ts` (5).
+
+### J-4 — `.xlsx` support is partial, and one screen claims `.xls` it cannot read. **OPEN (finding, no fix yet).**
+
+- Settings → Import data (`accept=".csv,.txt,.xlsx,.iif,.qbi,.vcf,…"`) does read `.xlsx` through
+  `parseExcelToRows` → `exceljs` (lazy `await import('exceljs')`, already in the bundle and excluded from
+  the PWA precache by `pwa-bundle-optimization.test.ts`). Good.
+- **`QBOMigrationWizard` accepts `.xls`** (`accept: { 'application/vnd.ms-excel': ['.xls', '.xlsx'] }`,
+  and its on-screen help says "Supports .csv, .xlsx, and .xls exports") but the parser is `exceljs`, which
+  **cannot read legacy BIFF `.xls`**. A user who drops a real `.xls` gets a raw parse error. Either the
+  claim goes or a converter is added — owner/lead decision.
+- Every other importer (bank statements, payroll provider CSV, price list, corporate card, GSA per diem,
+  migration trial balance proof, Xero documents) is CSV-only by design and says so in its own words; that
+  matches the queue text ("the importers" = the list importers), so no defect claimed.
+
+### J-6 — the invoice/statement PDF does **not** print the tax number or the customer's address. **OPEN (finding).**
+
+Executed the real generator (`generateDocumentPdf`, `src/server/services/pdfService.ts`) and read the PDF
+text back (`audit/agent11/probes/j6-invoice-pdf-content.ts`):
+
+- Workspace name ✔, workspace address ✔ (three lines), logo ✔ (`logoBytes(branding.logoDataUrl)`),
+  document number ✔, dates ✔, customer **name** ✔, Hebrew/bidi words ✔ (`מספר`, `תאריך`, `לתשלום עד`).
+- **Workspace tax number `515123456`: absent.** `layoutDocumentPdf` builds `company: { name, addressLines }`
+  only — there is no tax/VAT number field anywhere in the layout or the header.
+- **Customer address `1 Main St / Spring Valley NY 10977` and customer tax ID `12-3456789`: absent.**
+  The recipient block prints `doc.customerName` only (`recipient` at pdfService.ts:196-197); no address
+  lines, no customer tax id.
+- Long descriptions **do** wrap (`wrapText`, pdfText.ts) rather than being cut — queue item satisfied.
+- Side observation: with the fallback Helvetica font (embedded DejaVu missing) the probe showed mojibake
+  for `ILS 1,234.56`, `Short line` and some digits. The DejaVu fonts are committed
+  (`src/server/assets/fonts/`), so this is the documented no-font fallback, not a live defect — recorded
+  so nobody re-reports it as one.
+
+Severity: an Israeli tax invoice legally needs the supplier's ע.מ/ח.פ and, for a Tax Invoice to a
+business, the customer's name **and address**; a US invoice needs the seller's EIN on request. This is a
+**P1 for real bookkeeping**, not a Stage-A blocker. Not fixed here: PDF layout is AI #1's lane
+(`src/server/`), and the queue's J-6 explicitly says "report", not "patch the server".
+
+### J-7 — the Documents screen is weaker than the queue assumes. **OPEN (finding).**
+
+- There is no "documents browse" screen for attachments; the sidebar's **Documents** item is the
+  `vault` view (`src/components/forensics/Vault.tsx`), which lists only rows whose `uid` equals the
+  signed-in user (`where('uid','==',uid)` — attachments added by a colleague are invisible), filters by
+  tag only (**no type filter, no month filter**), shows the linked *transaction* (`linkedTransactionId`)
+  but not the invoice/bill/customer it belongs to (`linkedCollection`/`linkedLabel` are stored on the row
+  and never read by this screen), and has no error state (a failed snapshot just stops `loading`).
+  Cards are a decorative grid with no preview action. "Vault Depleted / Initialize upload to establish
+  audit compliance" is the empty state.
+- What *does* exist and works: `src/components/common/AttachmentsPanel.tsx` — per-record files with
+  preview (`attachmentPreviewKind` sandboxed to PDF/JPEG/PNG/WebP data URIs), download, remove with role
+  rules, 700 KB limit — mounted on invoices, bills, customers/vendors, credit notes, estimates, POs,
+  assets, inventory, workpapers and support tickets.
+So J-7 is real work: the filter-by-type/month, the "which entry or document", the preview in the list, and
+the empty/error split all still need building.
+
+### J-8 — "Download everything for a year" does not exist; the pieces do. **OPEN (finding).**
+
+- No screen or menu item contains any year-archive wording (grep over `src/`).
+- Building blocks already present: `buildWorkspaceArchive` (ZIP of every collection as JSON + CSV, from the
+  checksum-verified server backup, `src/lib/workspaceArchive.ts`), `AccountantExportPackView`
+  (`src/lib/accountantExportPack.ts`, own ZIP writer), `downloadCsv`, and the server PDF routes
+  (`documentRoutes.ts` zip of PDFs for a set of documents). A year-scoped archive is a composition job,
+  not new maths. Not started.
+
+## Status of the queue
+
+| Item | State at this checkpoint |
+|---|---|
+| J-1 export round trip | **Found + fixed + tested + pushed** (customers/vendors/items/accounts path). Still to check: bills export columns vs. any bill import (there is no bill list import — the bills `Export CSV` writes vendor/number/date/due/status/amount/currency and nothing reads it back; note for the list). |
+| J-2 import preview | Preview exists — **but shows 5 rows, not the 20 the queue asks for**, and refused rows are listed separately (200 cap) rather than marked *in* the preview. Finding recorded; small UI change, not started. |
+| J-3 duplicate check on contact import | **Already implemented** (`contactImportDuplicates`, shown on the screen with skip/possible-same lists). Gap vs. the queue: it is **informational only** — there is no skip / update / add-anyway choice, and no "update existing" path. Finding recorded. |
+| J-4 Excel files | `.xlsx` works on the list importers; the `.xls` claim in the QuickBooks wizard is false. Small fix, not started. |
+| J-5 Hebrew in exports | **Largely satisfied**: `downloadCsv` writes a UTF-8 BOM (`toCsv` does not); `workspaceArchive` and `accountantExportPack` prepend `\uFEFF` themselves. Gap: **no test asserts the BOM bytes or a Hebrew round trip**. Test to add. |
+| J-6 invoice PDF checks | **Finding: tax number and customer address missing** (report only, AI #1 lane). Wrapping verified good. |
+| J-7 attachments list | **Finding: no type/month filter, no owning document, no list preview, no error state, uid-scoped.** Not started. |
+| J-8 year-end archive | Not started; building blocks exist. |
+
+## Next actions (in order)
+
+1. Finish reading the full-suite result; record the exact counts.
+2. J-5: add the BOM/byte test and a Hebrew round-trip test (cheap, high value, pins behaviour that
+   currently has no test).
