Settings -> Backup & Export now has a year-end archive. src/lib/yearEndArchive.ts plans it purely
(recordYear over date/issueDate/documentDate/dueDate/createdAt; a record with no usable date is
counted as undated, never silently included; company-wide lists - customers, vendors, items,
accounts - are written whole because they carry no document date) and builds the CSV entries with
the shared writer and the J-5 UTF-8 marker. The screen reads the checksum-verified server backup
(the E-21 source, never the browser cache), shows the exact file list before anything downloads,
adds each invoice PDF from the existing document route, and zips with the existing stored-ZIP writer.

Tests: j8-year-end-archive 8/8 (file list, year scoping, undated count, invoice PDFs, ZIP round trip),
ledger-collections-guard 4/4, types and lint clean.

